# Valgavoth, Terror Eater's last ability refers only to the cards its own replacement effect exiled (CR 607.2b, 406.6).
# Bot1 has Leyline of the Void too, so each of Bot2's cards headed for Bot2's graveyard meets two replacement effects, and
# Bot2, whose card it is, chooses which applies (CR 616.1); once one has exiled it the other no longer applies. Bot2's
# Lightning Bolt goes by Leyline: exiled, but not with Valgavoth, so Bot1 can't cast it. Bot2's Shock goes by Valgavoth, and
# on turn 3 Bot1 casts it at Bot2 for 1 life, its mana value. Bot1 controlled that Shock, so Valgavoth lets it go to Bot2's graveyard, but
# Leyline (which asks nothing about control) exiles it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Leyline of the Void
Black Lotus x3
Valgavoth, Terror Eater
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Mox Ruby
Shock
Forest x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Valgavoth, Terror Eater.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Replace(Leyline of the Void)
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Shock.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Replace(Valgavoth, Terror Eater)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Exile = Lightning Bolt; Shock
! Bot1.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Exile.Shock.Cast(Bot2; Ability: 1 life)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Life = 14
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Exile = Lightning Bolt; Shock
